From b194ed86fb07a938522ca0ad4ca849ea94410c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:38:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Countdowns have priority: on the OLED's title row over
 everything, popups below them

A user's report: a gold knob's popup covered the countdown. Now, while a countdown runs, nothing covers it
(gui/ui/countdown.h). The countdowns: the song change's in the song browser while the song to come is armed (v14: the
loops, the bars of the last loop, the beats of the last bar), and the launch countdown in Song view (and the
performance view and the arranger, which draw through it) while clips or a section are armed to launch, counted as the
community firmware counted it there (the bars until the launch, in the last bar the beats; at least 1 until the launch).

OLED (OLED::sendMainImage()): the countdown is drawn last, over the finished image, on the title row (its label, the
number big on the right, the title's line under them), in a canvas of its own (overlayImage, which the CPU monitor's
line used alone before), so no screen's image is changed and it is gone the moment the countdown is. A popup that
would reach into the title row is moved down as far as the screen leaves room (a one-line popup entirely below it);
the CPU monitor's line goes to the bottom while a countdown takes the top. countdown::routine(), every UI tick (15 ms),
sends the OLED anew where the countdown's line has changed. The song browser no longer draws the countdown into its
image (LoadSongUI::displayCountdown(), removeCountdown()); Song view no longer draws 1.2.1's "Loops remaining: N" box
(SessionView::renderOLED()) nor the community's "Bars Remaining: N" box (displayLoopsRemainingPopup()), both in the
middle of the image, where every popup covered them: the song's name stays visible under the countdown.

7-segment display: while it shows a countdown, a gold knob turned or pressed or a mod button pressed shows no popup
(countdown::KnobPopupGuard in View::modEncoderAction(), modEncoderButtonAction(), modButtonAction();
display::popupsHeld in SevenSegment::displayPopup()); the knob still does all it does.

Tested (tests/songchange/songchange_emu.py, the firmware in the emulator): in the song browser while armed the upper
gold knob pressed (popup "HPF") and the DJ filter turned ("DJ: LPF 15"): the OLED's title row pixel for pixel as before,
the popup below it; on the 7-segment display the filter type changes and no popup comes; the countdown right in all
5,088 windows while armed; a new scenario launch: Song view, clips armed to stop after 2 loops, the countdown from 8 bars
to 1 beat on the title row in every window, a gold knob's value popup below it, the CPU monitor's line at the bottom,
nothing left after the launch. All six scenarios pass.

